# 31_ganzfeld_amber.ledc — Eyes-Closed Ganzfeld (Amber/Red), ~22 min — homogeneous field imagery
# Technique: playbook B7 "Ganzfeld: red bias, diffusion, ramps". A STEADY, uniform, warm
#            amber-red field viewed EYES CLOSED. The eyelid passes ~14.5% at 700 nm but
#            <=3% below 580 nm, so amber/red (>=620 nm) is the wavelength that actually
#            reaches the closed-eye retina. Homogeneous, unstructured stimulation (no flicker)
#            plus steady pink-noise 'shhh' induces the Ganzfeld effect — drifting imagery and
#            deep relaxation. A gentle 7 Hz theta binaural underlays it. This is the STEADY
#            FIELD complement to the cool-white FLICKER variant 15_ganzflicker_imagery.ledc.
# Bands: no visual flicker (steady field); 7 Hz theta binaural underlay; long stable hold.
#
# SAFETY / CONTRAINDICATIONS:
#   Do NOT use if you have photosensitive epilepsy, a seizure disorder, or a history of
#   photic migraine. Do not use while driving. Experiential, not medical.
#   The field is STEADY (freq 0, NO flicker) — the "no saturated-red strobe" rule concerns
#   FLICKERING red; a steady red field is safe. Brightness capped <=25%, eased IN over 15 s
#   (>=10 s rule) and faded out over 2 min. A hardware diffuser in front of the LEDs makes
#   the field more uniform (recommended for the true Ganzfeld effect).
#
# LED columns: time freq duty bright R G B mask   (freq 0 = steady amber-red field, mask 255)
# Audio: A time freq pan vol mod [ch] [freq_r] [wave]   (wave 5 pink; binaural via freq_r)
# Ramp convention = animate-on-start (the >/* prefix sits where a segment BEGINS).

# --- Ease-in (00:00-01:00): steady amber-red field + pink field + theta underlay fade in ---
0 0 100 >0 255 40 0 255           # steady amber-red field (>=620 nm); brightness ease-in from 0 (15 s)
A 0 200 0 >0 0 1 0 5              # ch1 pink-noise Ganzfeld field (auditory homogeneity); vol fade-in
A 0 253 0 >0 0 2 260 0           # ch2 binaural carrier 253 / R260 = 7 Hz theta underlay; vol fade-in
S 3000 default 65 "Eyes closed, gaze soft. Rest in the warm, even glow and the steady wash of sound."
15000 0 100 25 255 40 0 255       # brightness reaches 25% cap (>=10 s ease-in)
A 60000 200 0 45 0 1 0 5          # ch1 pink field settled 45
A 60000 253 0 25 0 2 260 0        # ch2 theta underlay settled 25

# --- Stable hold (01:00-20:00 = ~19 min): homogeneous field, no change ---
S 300000 default 65 "Let your eyes relax into the uniform field. Shapes and colours may begin to drift."
S 720000 default 65 "Nothing to seek. Just watch whatever arises in the glow."
S 1080000 default 65 "At ease, open, resting in the even light."

# --- Fade out (20:00-22:00): field + pink + underlay fade to 0 ---
1200000 0 100 >25 255 40 0 255    # brightness ramp-out START 25 ...
A 1200000 200 0 *45 0 1 0 5       # ch1 pink quad fade 45->0
A 1200000 253 0 *25 0 2 260 0     # ch2 theta quad fade 25->0
S 1200000 default 65 "Gently returning now. Let the glow and the sound fade away."
1320000 0 100 0 255 40 0 255      # end: brightness 0
A 1320000 200 0 0 0 1 0 5         # end: pink vol 0
A 1320000 253 0 0 0 2 260 0       # end: theta vol 0
